    "id": "prop:three-cell-five-arm-audit",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "In \\(\\mathsf E_{3,5}\\), the policywise widths \\((R_{\\pi_1}(S),R_{\\pi_2}(S))\\) and worst widths \\(\\overline W(S)\\) for all \\(|S|\\leq2\\) are: \\(\\varnothing:(1,1;1)\\); \\(\\{c_1\\}:(1/2,7/8;7/8)\\); \\(\\{c_2\\}:(1/6,5/8;5/8)\\); \\(\\{c_3\\}:(7/8,1/2;7/8)\\); \\(\\{c_4\\}:(5/8,1/6;5/8)\\); \\(\\{c_5\\}:(3/4,1;1)\\); \\(\\{c_1,c_2\\}:(0,1/2;1/2)\\); \\(\\{c_1,c_3\\}:(1/2,1/2;1/2)\\); \\(\\{c_1,c_4\\}:(1/8,1/24;1/8)\\); \\(\\{c_1,c_5\\}:(1/2,7/8;7/8)\\); \\(\\{c_2,c_3\\}:(1/24,1/8;1/8)\\); \\(\\{c_2,c_4\\}:(1/6,1/6;1/6)\\); \\(\\{c_2,c_5\\}:(1/6,5/8;5/8)\\); \\(\\{c_3,c_4\\}:(1/2,0;1/2)\\); \\(\\{c_3,c_5\\}:(5/8,1/2;5/8)\\); and \\(\\{c_4,c_5\\}:(3/8,1/6;3/8)\\). Hence \\(D^{\\star}=1/8\\), attained by \\(\\{c_1,c_4\\}\\) and \\(\\{c_2,c_3\\}\\), and the mixed-integer optimum is \\(1/8\\). For the displayed table under \\(S^{\\star}=\\{c_1,c_4\\}\\), the two displayed schedules are compatible members of \\(\\mathcal M_N\\), are observationally indistinguishable, and attain simultaneously \\([L(\\pi_1),U(\\pi_1)]=[0,1/8]\\) and \\([L(\\pi_2),U(\\pi_2)]=[1/8,1/6]\\). Finally \\(\\mathsf{Check}(S^{\\star},1/8,\\mathcal T_{3,5})=\\mathrm{true}\\).",
